{% comment %}
  The product page (Figma: Standart Product Page, node 2032:3113).

  The section owns the page geometry and the media: the trail above the title, the
  two columns, and the framed gallery with its thumbnails. Everything down the
  right-hand side is a block, so the merchant reorders the price and the rating,
  drops the gift message card, or adds a fourth detail card without a deploy. See
  `docs/section-settings.md`.

  Built from the kit throughout — ui-product-gallery, ui-breadcrumb, and through the
  blocks ui-variant-select, ui-quantity-stepper, ui-button, ui-panel, ui-tag and
  ui-message. Horizon's own product blocks are untouched and unused here.

  This one is wired, which most of the kit is not. Choosing a variant re-fetches the
  product and Horizon's `<variant-picker>` fires `variant:update`; the price block,
  the buy block and the gallery each answer it. Add to cart posts through
  `<product-form-component>`. The details of that seam are in
  `snippets/ui-product-variant-picker.liquid` and `blocks/_ui-product-buy.liquid`,
  where they can be read next to the markup they explain.

  Three column arrangements, not two. The file draws 630 and 586 side by side at
  1440 and draws no phone at all. Held down to 750px those two columns leave the
  details about 300px, which is narrower than the buy row's own controls, so the
  page stacks below 990px and takes a tighter gap between 990 and 1200. Inside the
  details column nothing else needs a breakpoint: the buy row and the reassurance
  grid give way on their own, which they have to, since the width they get is a
  share of a grid and not a share of the viewport.

  The badge on the gallery comes from the product's tags, matched against the list
  in the theme's Product badges settings — the same list the product cards read.
  One list, every place a badge appears.

  The breadcrumb steps through the collection the shopper arrived from when there is
  one, and the product's first collection otherwise. One step, not all of them: a
  product filed under six collections would otherwise print a trail longer than its
  own title.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign product_resource = product
  if request.visual_preview_mode and product_resource == blank
    assign product_resource = collections.all.products.first
  endif

  assign crumb_source = product_resource.collections
  if collection != blank
    assign from_collection = product_resource.collections | where: 'handle', collection.handle
    if from_collection.size > 0
      assign crumb_source = from_collection
    endif
  endif

  assign crumbs = ''
  if crumb_source.size > 0
    assign crumbs = crumb_source | slice: 0, 1
  endif

-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The gallery badge reads the same tag list the product cards read, so a product
  tagged Bestsellers says so on the card and again on its own page without the
  shop stating it twice. `show_badge` still decides whether this page shows it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture page_badge -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_badge -%}
    {% render 'ui-product-badge', product: product_resource %}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign page_badge_parts = page_badge | strip | split: '|' -%}

<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} spacing-style color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  data-testid="product-main-{{ section.id }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div
    class="product-main product-main--media-{{ section.settings.media_position }}"
    style="
      --product-main-column-gap: {{ section.settings.column_gap }}px;
      --product-main-details-gap: {{ section.settings.details_gap }}px;
    "
  >
    {%- if section.settings.show_breadcrumb -%}
      {% render 'ui-breadcrumb', links: crumbs, current: product_resource.title, class: 'product-main__breadcrumb' %}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="product-main__layout">
      <div class="product-main__media">
        {% render 'ui-product-gallery',
          product: product_resource,
          badge: page_badge_parts[0],
          badge_tone: page_badge_parts[1],
          eager: true
        %}
      </div>

      <div class="product-main__details">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .product-main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .product-main__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .product-main__details {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--product-main-details-gap, 24px);

    /*
     * A query container, so a block inside can answer to the width of this column
     * rather than to the viewport's. The two are not the same thing here: the
     * column is one track of a grid above 990px and the whole page below it, so a
     * viewport breakpoint tells a block almost nothing about the room it has.
     * `base.css` already leans on this for its resource lists.
     */
    container-type: inline-size;

    /*
     * The contract the rule block reads, so a hairline can sit at the 20px the file
     * draws inside a column set 24px apart. A block cannot shrink a parent's gap;
     * it can only measure against it. See blocks/_ui-rule.liquid.
     */
    --ui-stack-gap: var(--product-main-details-gap, 24px);

    /* The file sets the rating's stars 4px from its wording, where the kit's own
       default is the 8px the hero wants. */
    --ui-review-line-inline-gap: 4px;
  }

  /*
   * Two columns only once there is room for both. At 990px the details column is
   * about 425px, which still holds the buy row; at 750px it would be near 300px,
   * where the quantity stepper alone takes 132 of it.
   */
  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .product-main__layout {
      /* The drawn proportion, not a setting: 630 and 586 either side of the gap. */
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 630fr) minmax(0, 586fr);
      /*
       * Held at 40 until the page is wide enough to spare the rest. base.css steps
       * the gutter from 40 to 80 a side at 1200px, so the content column loses 80px
       * there on its own; a gap that widened at the same point took another 24 on
       * top and the details column came out *narrower* at 1200 than at 1199, with
       * the buy row breaking to two lines as the window got bigger. `min()` so a
       * merchant who asks for less than 40 still gets it.
       */
      column-gap: min(var(--product-main-column-gap, 64px), 40px);
    }

    .product-main--media-right .product-main__layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 586fr) minmax(0, 630fr);
    }

    .product-main--media-right .product-main__media {
      order: 2;
    }
  }

  /* The drawn 64px, at the width it is drawn at. By 1400 the content column has
     stopped growing, so the gap is spending width the columns no longer need. */
  @media screen and (min-width: 1400px) {
    .product-main__layout {
      column-gap: var(--product-main-column-gap, 64px);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product page",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_breadcrumb",
      "label": "Show the trail above the title",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.media"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_position",
      "label": "Position",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "left",
          "label": "t:options.left"
        },
        {
          "value": "right",
          "label": "t:options.right"
        }
      ],
      "default": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_badge",
      "label": "Show the badge",
      "info": "Set by the product's tags, against the list in Theme settings \u2192 Product badges.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "column_gap",
      "label": "t:settings.gap",
      "info": "Between the media and the details, from 1400px up. Below that it holds at 40px, where the page has less width to spare.",
      "min": 24,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "details_gap",
      "label": "Space between details",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:settings.width",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "page-width",
          "label": "t:options.page"
        },
        {
          "value": "full-width",
          "label": "t:options.full"
        }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:settings.color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 32
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
